      "notes": "Berkeley County WV (Martinsburg; FIPS 54003) uses the statewide WV parcel layer hosted by the WV GIS Technical Center (WVGISTC) at WVU (services.wvgis.wvu.edu), the same layer as Kanawha, Monongalia, Raleigh and Cabell. CRITICAL: the county code is the state's own alphabetical number, a zero-padded 2-digit string ('02' for Berkeley, NOT the FIPS digits '003' and NOT an integer); use WHERE COUNTY='02' (or CountyID='02') with quotes. COUNTY and CountyID agree on all 62,652 Berkeley rows. 2026-10-10: 62,652 rows. Owner is populated on 62,022 rows (99.0%), situs on 61,589 (98.3%) and mailing on 62,022 (99.0%). Situs contains MARTINSBURG on 8 rows and PARKERSBURG (a Wood County city) on none; most situs values are the street only, so the city is a weak check. No owner, situs or mailing value carries an asterisk or a placeholder token. The layer description says the service was 'updated for Tax Year 2023', so ownership can trail the county's own roll by years, and the layer publishes no per-row date. Key fields: CleanParcelID (20-digit: CountyID-District-Map-ParcelPrefix-ParcelSuffix-SpecialID), FullOwnerName, FullOwnerAddress, FullPhysicalAddress, FullLegalDescription, GISPID, CountyID, COUNTY, CALC_ACRE. The layer allows 2,000 rows per page with pagination and answers cross-origin requests (the server echoes the request Origin). Verified 2026-10-10 with an Origin: https://urbankitstudio.com header: an owner SMITH search matches 618 rows and a MAIN ST situs search 32; the control county Kanawha (COUNTY '20') answers the same queries with 114,951 rows and 113,891 owners.",
