      "notes": "Wood County WV (Parkersburg; FIPS 54107) uses the statewide WV parcel layer hosted by the WV GIS Technical Center (WVGISTC) at WVU (services.wvgis.wvu.edu), the same layer as Kanawha, Monongalia, Raleigh and Cabell. CRITICAL: the county code is the state's own alphabetical number, a zero-padded 2-digit string ('54' for Wood, NOT the FIPS digits '107' and NOT an integer); use WHERE COUNTY='54' (or CountyID='54') with quotes. COUNTY and CountyID agree on all 58,263 Wood rows. 2026-10-10: 58,263 rows. Owner is populated on 58,261 rows (100.00%), situs on 58,159 (99.8%) and mailing on 58,002 (99.6%). Situs contains PARKERSBURG on 21 rows and MARTINSBURG (a Berkeley County city) on none; most situs values are the street only, so the city is a weak check. 263 mailing values carry asterisks: 251 of them are fully masked, asterisks standing in for the street and city (some keep the ZIP, some carry none), and the atlas serves them as no mailing address; the other 12 are real addresses and are served. 20 other mailing values read 'UNKNOWN,'. 6 owner rows carry a trailing asterisk on a real name. The layer description says the service was 'updated for Tax Year 2023', so ownership can trail the county's own roll by years, and the layer publishes no per-row date. Key fields: CleanParcelID (20-digit: CountyID-District-Map-ParcelPrefix-ParcelSuffix-SpecialID), FullOwnerName, FullOwnerAddress, FullPhysicalAddress, FullLegalDescription, GISPID, CountyID, COUNTY, CALC_ACRE. The layer allows 2,000 rows per page with pagination and answers cross-origin requests (the server echoes the request Origin). Verified 2026-10-10 with an Origin: https://urbankitstudio.com header: an owner SMITH search matches 845 rows and a MAIN ST situs search 43; the control county Kanawha (COUNTY '20') answers the same queries with 114,951 rows and 113,891 owners.",
